(def ^:private apple-simdgroup-flip-note
  "THIS VARIANT'S OWN FLIP CELLS (ADR-0373's flip contract applied to
  :simdgroup-reduce's own measured cells, 2026-10-23/24, JUN-58): the
  conforming channel (ADR-0360 question (1)'s native-Metal harness
  family, the emitters' own bytes) measured :baseline vs
  :simdgroup-reduce at SIX cells -- W = 256 (the honesty-lock flip
  anchor) and W = 512, W = 1024, W = 128, W = 64 and W = 32 (the
  W-sweep
  series' second through sixth
  cells), all
  n = 1000003 (the flip contract's ground shape) -- on the
  tested device class (name fragment \"m1 max\", reported subgroup size
  32), the historical protocol unchanged (6 fresh processes, 20
  interleaved AB/BA pairs per operator per run, 2 warmups discarded,
  verified read-back). Paired median ratios (:simdgroup-reduce /
  :baseline gpu ns): W = 256 -- :sum 0.790, :max 0.800, :min 0.799;
  W = 512 -- :sum 0.815, :max 0.823, :min 0.824;
  W = 1024 -- :sum 0.840, :max 0.847, :min 0.850;
  W = 128 -- :sum 0.775, :max 0.789, :min 0.789;
  W = 64 -- :sum 0.719, :max 0.728, :min 0.729;
  W = 32 -- :sum 0.657, :max 0.658, :min 0.650. The contrast with
  :subgroup-reduce at the identical cells takes TWO forms and only the
  WEAKER one reaches W = 32: the stronger form (both folds one-sided,
  opposite signs) holds at W = 64/128/256/512/1024 (~1.22 at W = 256,
  1.196/1.195/1.197 at W = 512, 1.186/1.186/1.185 at W = 1024,
  1.244/1.243/1.234 at W = 128, 1.218/1.216/1.214 at W = 64), while at
  W = 32 the shuffle ladder measures MIXED (0.918/0.923/1.019 -- the
  min operator's per-run ratios straddle 1.0, that cell's verdict is
  regime-scoped) and only THIS fold is one-sided there. At all six
  cells THIS variant's own claim-protocol rule-2 verdict is
  REGIME-INVARIANT FASTER (18/18 per-run ratios below 1.0 at each
  cell, every observed regime one-sided -- at W = 32 including the
  returned fresh-process fast level), so each cell is a selection
  basis on its own measurement; the W = 32 flip rests on this fold's
  18/18, not on the contrast. Measurement beats the
  carve-out's earlier decision exactly here: the cells answer
  :simdgroup-reduce with
  :measured? true. The six are every width the row admits (a power of
  two in [32, 1024]): the class's W band is flipped end to end and its
  advantage is monotone across it in these records (0.65 -> 0.72 ->
  0.78 -> 0.79 -> 0.82 -> 0.84 with W -- data on one host, not a fitted
  trend and not a claim about any unmeasured W or any other shape).
  SHAPE-2 FLIP OF THE W = 256 CELL (the shape-2 series' anchor,
  2026-10-24, apple-simdgroup-shape2-flip-note): the same byte-identical
  protocol re-ran W = 256 at shape 2, n = 2^20 (a clean multiple of every
